      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Consider the following system of equations. \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-5x+y=8 \\\\ 8x-7y=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDescribe the steps needed to eliminate the variable $y$ from the system:\n\nTo eliminate $y,$ multiply the \n{{field-1}} \nequation by \n{{field-2}}, \nand add the equations.",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the coefficient of $y$ in the first equation is $1,$ while in the second equation it is $-7.$ \n\nIf we multiply the first equation by $7,$ then the coefficient of $y$ will turn into $7,$ which will cancel with the coefficient of $-7$ in the second equation.\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}(\\,-5x+y=8\\,)\\,\\times (7) \\\\ 8x-7y=25\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,\\{\\begin{aligned}-35x+7y=56 \\\\ 8x-7y=25\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, when we add the two equations, the variable $y$ will be eliminated:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-35x+\\cancel{7y} & =56 \\\\ 8x-\\cancel{7y} & =25 \\\\ (-35x+8x) & =(56+25) \\\\ -27x & =81\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the following:\n\n*To eliminate $y,$ multiply the $\\text{first}$ equation by $7,$ and add the equations*.",
